Skip dladdr in GetRuntimePath on wasi.

Env::GetRuntimePath uses dladdr() to find the directory of the onnxruntime
binary, in order to locate provider shared libraries next to it. wasix's dyld
provides dlopen/dlsym/dlclose but no dladdr, so the module fails to load
("Dynamically-linked symbol not found: dladdr"). Our build is static with a
single CPU EP and loads no provider .so, so take the existing non-dladdr
fallback (as AIX already does).

Upstream fix: also guard the dladdr path on __wasi__.

diff --git a/onnxruntime/core/platform/posix/env.cc b/onnxruntime/core/platform/posix/env.cc
--- a/onnxruntime/core/platform/posix/env.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/platform/posix/env.cc
@@ -569,8 +569,8 @@ class PosixEnv : public Env {
   }

   PathString GetRuntimePath() const override {
-// In AIX, dladdr is not supported.
-#if !defined(_AIX)
+// In AIX, dladdr is not supported. wasix's dyld provides no dladdr either.
+#if !defined(_AIX) && !defined(__wasi__)
     // Use dladdr() to look up the file that contains an address from this binary.
     const void* const address_from_this_binary = reinterpret_cast<const void*>(Env::Default);

